# Netlify redirects.
#
# Format:  <from-path>  <to-path>  <status>
# One rule per line; add new lines at the bottom. Rules are matched top to
# bottom, first match wins.
#
# Netlify serves these at the CDN edge, before the request reaches Next, so
# they win over next.config.js redirects and over the SSR 404 handler. The
# trailing "!" forces the rule, which is what makes it beat that handler.
#
# Note: these cannot be tested with `npm run dev` - there is no Netlify edge in
# front of it, so the file is simply never read. Use `npx netlify dev`, or
# verify on a deploy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Old category-path URLs -> /blog/<slug>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Posts used to live under /creative-experiences-behind-the-image/<slug>. They
# now live under /blog/<slug>, so the old paths 404. These rules point the
# links that are already out in the world (newsletters, search results) at the
# posts' current homes.

# "5 Dragon Women" was also renamed - the piece covers six women - so the slug
# changed as well as the prefix.
